The grade will be distributed on:
- A word report
- A final presentation
- Weekly progress & presentations

Phase 1:
- Literature review : present your idea, previous ideas similar to it (existing solutions), and how your solution differs (what advantage does it add?)
- Motivation: why did you chose this idea? what particular strength does it offer? what are the disadvantages of previous solutions?
- Choose the optimal solution based on your research and study

Design Process:
- Build a simluation on proteus. Test it 10 times with different inputs. Analyze outputs and make sure it works correclty. Identify possible issues and solve them
- Build a prototype. Test it 10 times, in different use cases and environments

Notes:
- You need to understand the problem from all perspectives in order to deliver the best solution
- You need to choose every component for a reason and be able to explain it

Choosing components:
- Research available options, compare them, and choose based on your specific use case
- Take into consideration : time sensitiveness, output accuracy, budget, etc.. ( more accurate sensors cost more)

Presentation:
- Practice as much as you can. The jury will ask you questions and evaluate your work based on how you present it
